  "body": "What happens: `model::set_facets` bumps an entity's geometry revision (`rev`) on every landing. The project loader pins `rev` back to the file's value for **models** (`project/apply.rs`, the `EntityKind::Model` arm, \"the loader's pin is UNCONDITIONAL (M5.3 A)\"), but the `EntityKind::Stock` arm calls `set_facets` and never pins. So a stock edited twice (e.g. `SetStock` twice) saves `\"rev\": 2`, loads as rev 1, and the re-save differs from the file it was opened from.\n\nExpected: a stock's `rev` survives save/load like a model's (pin it after the stock arm's `set_facets`).\n\nEvidence: found while working #326 - `AlignPartToSetup` re-meshed a box stock it had only moved and the round-trip test saw `\"rev\": 2` vs `\"rev\": 1` on the `Stock` entity. #326 now only re-meshes a stock whose size changed, which side-steps it; the loader gap itself is untouched. Staleness never reads `rev` (the stamp's signature does), so this is file-byte churn, not a wrong path.\n\nDone means: save -> load -> save of a document whose stock was set twice is byte-identical, pinned by a project_roundtrip test.\n",
